        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Bulawayo Railway Museum, Cape Colony, South Africa\n- People: Cecil Rhodes, Cecil John Rhodes\n- Organizations: Privy Council\n- Roles: Prime Minister of the Cape Colony\n- Topics: railway exhibits, personal railway coach\n\nFacts:\n- Cecil John Rhodes was born on 5 July 1853 and died on 26 March 1902.\n- Cecil John Rhodes was a British businessman, mining magnate, and politician in South Africa.\n- Cecil Rhodes served as Prime Minister of the Cape Colony from 1890 to 1896.\n- The oldest exhibits at the Bulawayo Railway Museum date back to 1897.\n- The Bulawayo Railway Museum includes Cecil Rhodes' personal railway coach among its oldest exhibits.",
